    "hypothesis": "Fuse ALPH filtering/normalization and transform-family analysis. Accumulate green, green-difference and sketch banks once; reconstruct invariant/permuted banks once instead of repeating per-pixel full-color work and a second full-frame scan.",
    "endState": "Keep the full13-bank canonical representation and one existing final selector/geometry implementation. Separate normalized mixed-color and fused ALPH entry points share prepared-candidate execution and seed ownership. No new owner/cache/pool/session or per-pixel generic dispatch.",
    "identity": "For each included normalizedgreen pixel, A/R/B and their differences are0. Nonzero red/blue subtract-green banks are permutations of green by i -> (-i)&255; difference banks are the same permutation of green differences. A/R/B zero bins each equal the number of included pixels. Preserve the exact first-pixel and above/previous skip, sketch, all pseudocounts, entropy arithmetic, candidate order and ties.",
    "costScope": "Complete513x259Q75/effort4 alpha8 encode first; reuse frozen complete packets and representative original control. Alpha16 and same actual package qualification only at acceptance. Allocation savings are not CPU proof.",
    "invalidation": "Common final selector is outlined for both generic and fused analysis: all six current VP8L and two ALPH complete costs are affected; opaqueVP8, other codecs/resizing/text remain unchanged. Refresh these8existing costs only at acceptance; unchanged correctness/package evidence is reused until an accepted production milestone.",
    "temporaryState": "Generic Select remains the mixed-color production implementation and test oracle. Duplicated final selection is forbidden; any temporary duplication is removed before a completed stage. Failure/refusal never falls back to generic selection.",
    "continuation": "Focused field/output identity and ownership on bothOS/scalar, then bounded complete short; independent confirmation only if useful. Keep adverse evidence. Revise or restore if complete benefit does not justify complexity.",
